{"id": "nursing-homes-money-out-staff-short", "title": "Nursing homes: $1.02 billion owed by related companies at 42 Bay Area homes", "seconds": 134.9, "voice": "elevenlabs:OtHu0lbpdNTqJVqaxDtR", "narrator": "Maven", "tempo": 1.2, "made": "2026-11-25", "key": "cca05ad09b95b84f", "words": 399, "beats": [{"scene": "open", "kind": "chain", "ref": ["story[0]", "suspicious[0].why"], "text": "Many nursing homes share an owner with their landlord and manager.", "t0": 0.2, "t1": 2.96, "shot": "b0", "visual": {"type": "chain", "steps": [{"art": "housing", "name": "Nursing home", "sub": "reports to the State"}, {"art": "money", "name": "Money owed to it", "sub": "by related companies"}, {"art": "contract", "name": "Related companies", "sub": "same owner"}], "kicker": "How it works"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.19, 0.48, 0.8, 1.05, 1.14, 1.38, 1.51, 1.68, 2.11, 2.22]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "chain", "ref": ["story[0]", "suspicious[0].why"], "text": "Each year, a home reports what those related companies owe it.", "t0": 3.08, "t1": 5.77, "shot": "b0", "visual": {"type": "chain", "steps": [{"art": "housing", "name": "Nursing home", "sub": "reports to the State"}, {"art": "money", "name": "Money owed to it", "sub": "by related companies"}, {"art": "contract", "name": "Related companies", "sub": "same owner"}], "kicker": "How it works"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.19, 0.48, 0.59, 0.79, 1.11, 1.25, 1.45, 1.79, 2.26, 2.46]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["oneLine", "amount", "suspicious[0]"], "text": "In 42 Bay Area homes, that’s half of everything they own. How much in all?", "t0": 5.89, "t1": 10.78, "shot": "b1", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "question", "label": "42 of 183 Bay Area homes", "sub": "half or more of their assets owed by related companies"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.17, 0.65, 0.87, 1.21, 1.81, 2.12, 2.4, 2.56, 2.91, 3.13, 3.58, 4.17, 4.38, 4.52]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["amount", "suspicious[0]"], "text": "1.02 billion dollars.", "t0": 10.78, "t1": 13.7, "shot": "b2", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$1.02 billion", "label": "owed to 42 homes by related companies"}, "emph": ["1.02"], "wt": [0.04, 0.7, 1.03, 1.32, 1.66, 2.31]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "caveat", "ref": ["caveat", "story[6]"], "text": "It’s a lead, not a finding.", "t0": 14.22, "t1": 15.92, "shot": "b3", "visual": {"type": "caveat", "line": "This is a lead, not a finding: a pattern in public records. This film says what the records show, what they do not show, and what would settle it."}, "wt": [0.0, 0.17, 0.27, 0.9, 1.03, 1.12]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "caveat", "ref": ["caveat", "story[6]"], "text": "These deals are disclosed, and the money can be pooled cash.", "t0": 16.04, "t1": 18.59, "shot": "b3", "visual": {"type": "caveat", "line": "This is a lead, not a finding: a pattern in public records. This film says what the records show, what they do not show, and what would settle it."}, "wt": [0.0, 0.18, 0.43, 0.59, 1.15, 1.22, 1.3, 1.5, 1.62, 1.7, 2.03]}, {"scene": "found", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[0].why", "established[0]", "established[1]"], "text": "So what does owed mean here?", "t0": 18.81, "t1": 20.27, "shot": "b4", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "value the home has passed to them and not yet got back"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.08, 0.23, 0.45, 0.77, 1.04]}, {"scene": "found", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[0].why", "established[0]", "established[1]"], "text": "It means the home sent value to the owner’s other companies, and hasn’t got it back.", "t0": 20.27, "t1": 24.61, "shot": "b4", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "value the home has passed to them and not yet got back"}, "wt": [0.04, 0.43, 0.61, 0.73, 1.04, 1.25, 1.57, 1.68, 1.78, 2.23, 2.45, 3.08, 3.37, 3.65, 3.82, 3.93]}, {"scene": "found", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["established[8]"], "text": "On the record, federal fines: 60 homes looked at here carry 3.4 million.", "t0": 24.73, "t1": 29.7, "shot": "b26", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "gavel", "label": "Federal fines", "kicker": "On the record", "sub": "60 homes, $3.4 million", "chip": "$1.2 million"}, "emph": ["3.4 million"], "wt": [0.0, 0.06, 0.16, 0.54, 0.84, 1.41, 2.3, 2.6, 2.82, 2.95, 3.17, 3.54, 3.76, 4.07, 4.24]}, {"scene": "found", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["established[8]"], "text": "The largest, 1.2 million, is Laguna Honda Hospital, in San Francisco.", "t0": 29.82, "t1": 33.64, "shot": "b26", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "gavel", "label": "Federal fines", "kicker": "On the record", "sub": "60 homes, $3.4 million", "chip": "$1.2 million"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.07, 0.58, 0.73, 1.03, 1.14, 1.63, 1.73, 2.12, 2.4, 2.97, 3.06, 3.26]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[0].what"], "text": "The first lead is size. Garfield Neurobehavioral Center, in Oakland, is owed 33.6 million.", "t0": 33.86, "t1": 39.87, "shot": "b5", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "housing", "label": "Garfield Neurobehavioral Center", "kicker": "The first lead", "sub": "Oakland, 2025", "chip": "$33.6 million"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.05, 0.31, 0.52, 0.7, 1.29, 1.97, 2.66, 3.12, 3.26, 3.98, 4.11, 4.32, 4.85, 5.16, 5.47]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[0].what"], "text": "What share of all it owns?", "t0": 39.99, "t1": 41.35, "shot": "b5", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "housing", "label": "Garfield Neurobehavioral Center", "kicker": "The first lead", "sub": "Oakland, 2025", "chip": "$33.6 million"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.18, 0.44, 0.58, 0.78, 0.93]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[0].what"], "text": "87 percent.", "t0": 41.35, "t1": 43.14, "shot": "b6", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "87%", "label": "of its assets, owed by related companies", "sub": "3.3 times a year’s revenue"}, "emph": ["87"], "wt": [0.04, 1.23]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[0].what"], "text": "Three such homes are in San Francisco, owed 63.4 million.", "t0": 43.66, "t1": 47.86, "shot": "b7", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$63.4 million", "label": "owed to 3 San Francisco homes"}, "emph": ["63.4 million"], "wt": [0.0, 0.24, 0.49, 0.69, 0.81, 0.91, 1.1, 2.04, 2.3, 2.86, 3.22, 3.38]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["established[5]"], "text": "And in 2025 the 42 homes paid related companies 71 million.", "t0": 47.98, "t1": 53.13, "shot": "b7x", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$71.0 million", "label": "paid to related companies by the 42 homes, 2025"}, "emph": ["71 million"], "wt": [0.0, 0.06, 0.18, 0.39, 1.13, 1.52, 1.94, 2.27, 2.53, 2.86, 3.35, 4.08]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[3]", "story[3]"], "text": "The second lead is staff: nurse hours per resident, per day.", "t0": 53.35, "t1": 56.63, "shot": "b8", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "magnifier", "label": "Nurse hours per resident day", "kicker": "The second lead"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.05, 0.32, 0.52, 0.68, 1.52, 1.79, 2.06, 2.26, 2.85, 3.01]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[3]", "story[3]"], "text": "California’s middle is 4.25. The lowest Bay Area home?", "t0": 56.75, "t1": 60.83, "shot": "b8", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "magnifier", "label": "Nurse hours per resident day", "kicker": "The second lead"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.49, 0.79, 0.95, 1.11, 1.4, 1.51, 2.15, 2.9, 3.24, 3.43, 3.65]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[3].what"], "text": "2.49.", "t0": 60.83, "t1": 62.21, "shot": "b9", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "2.49", "label": "Inspire Behavioral Health, San Jose", "sub": "Bay Area middle: 4.19"}, "emph": ["2.49"], "wt": [0.04, 0.51, 0.88, 1.08]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[3].what"], "text": "22 homes had days with residents and no registered nurse.", "t0": 62.73, "t1": 66.12, "shot": "b10", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "calendar", "label": "No registered nurse", "kicker": "The second lead", "sub": "22 homes, up to 98 days"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.51, 0.78, 0.99, 1.23, 1.39, 1.92, 2.13, 2.31, 2.8]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[1]"], "text": "The third lead puts both together.", "t0": 66.34, "t1": 68.05, "shot": "b11", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["below 4.25 nurse hours", "22 homes"], "b": ["owed by related companies", "$352.9 million"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.09, 0.38, 0.73, 1.09, 1.29]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[1]"], "text": "How many fall below the middle and are owed the most?", "t0": 68.17, "t1": 71.02, "shot": "b11", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["below 4.25 nurse hours", "22 homes"], "b": ["owed by related companies", "$352.9 million"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.08, 0.3, 0.57, 0.88, 1.02, 1.29, 1.48, 1.62, 1.79, 1.92]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[1]"], "text": "22.", "t0": 71.02, "t1": 71.69, "shot": "b12", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "22", "label": "homes on both lists", "sub": "$352.9 million owed, $85.1 million net income"}, "emph": ["22"], "wt": [0.04]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[1].what", "suspicious[1].why"], "text": "They’re owed 352.9 million.", "t0": 72.21, "t1": 74.75, "shot": "b13", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "gavel", "label": "41 citations or penalties", "kicker": "The third lead", "sub": "2019 to June 2024, 16 for nursing hours"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.12, 0.35, 0.51, 0.85, 1.41, 1.83, 2.0]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[1].what", "suspicious[1].why"], "text": "The State cited them 41 times, 16 of them for nursing hours.", "t0": 74.87, "t1": 78.94, "shot": "b13", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "gavel", "label": "41 citations or penalties", "kicker": "The third lead", "sub": "2019 to June 2024, 16 for nursing hours"}, "emph": ["41 times"], "wt": [0.0, 0.11, 0.39, 0.71, 0.92, 1.49, 2.38, 2.78, 2.91, 3.1, 3.24, 3.61]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[1].why", "established[9]"], "text": "Other Bay Area homes fall below the middle just as often. One doesn’t predict the other.", "t0": 79.06, "t1": 83.39, "shot": "b13b", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["homes with large related balances", "22 of 42, 52%"], "b": ["other Bay Area homes", "75 of 146, 51%"], "kicker": "Below the California middle"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.18, 0.39, 0.67, 1.04, 1.23, 1.43, 1.57, 1.87, 2.18, 2.33, 2.88, 3.37, 3.64, 3.95, 4.05]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["established[11]", "innocent[5]"], "text": "Allegations tell a milder story: 3,180 at the 42 homes, under the State average.", "t0": 83.51, "t1": 89.37, "shot": "b13c", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "3,180", "label": "complaint and incident allegations at the 42 homes, 2023 to 2025", "sub": "against 5,033 at the State average"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.69, 0.88, 0.95, 1.32, 2.21, 2.36, 2.78, 3.01, 3.23, 3.56, 3.67, 3.76, 4.24, 4.87, 5.02, 5.15, 5.37]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[2]"], "text": "The fourth lead is one chain. PACS Group has 31 Bay Area homes.", "t0": 89.59, "t1": 94.27, "shot": "b14", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "contract", "label": "PACS Group", "kicker": "The fourth lead", "sub": "31 Bay Area homes, $436.0 million owed"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.11, 0.39, 0.67, 0.87, 1.13, 2.17, 2.71, 2.97, 3.11, 3.6, 3.87, 4.2]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[2]"], "text": "What share of their assets is owed to them?", "t0": 94.39, "t1": 95.98, "shot": "b14", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "contract", "label": "PACS Group", "kicker": "The fourth lead", "sub": "31 Bay Area homes, $436.0 million owed"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.29, 0.39, 0.5, 0.89, 1.01, 1.2, 1.28]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[2]"], "text": "78 percent.", "t0": 95.98, "t1": 97.5, "shot": "b15", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "78%", "label": "of PACS homes’ assets"}, "emph": ["78"], "wt": [0.04, 0.99]}, {"scene": "lead5", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[4]", "established[2]"], "text": "The last lead: the State’s Medicaid fraud unit.", "t0"